    "body": "### What happens?\n\nThe distinct function is not retrieving unique values. I have to rely on Group by, any ideas?\n\n\nselect \ndistinct  [Varcharfield]  as field\nfrom [table] \n\nvs \n\nselect \n[Varcharfield]  as field\nfrom [table] \ngroup by  [Varcharfield]\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\nNo package imports. The table was extracted in from a sql server 2016 database. \n\nDB collation: Latin1_General_CI_AS\n\nselect \ndistinct  [Varcharfield]  as field\nfrom [table] \n\nvs \n\nselect \n[Varcharfield]  as field\nfrom [table] \ngroup by  [Varcharfield]\n\n### OS:\n\nWindows\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nDuckDB UI\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nmarce\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nNA\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [ ] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNo - Other reason (please specify in the issue body)",
